  "body": "Secure your slice of sought-after Eastern Beach! Positioned on a flat 459 square metre freehold site, 5A Rogers Avenue backs onto Macleans Reserve and is just a short stroll from the beach. This little gem offers a coastal lifestyle to enjoy now, with exciting possibilities for the future.\r\n\r\nIn zone for Macleans College, Bucklands Beach Intermediate and Bucklands Beach Primary School, the location is a real drawcard for families and buyers looking to build their next home.\r\n\r\nCompact yet practical, this home was built in 2011 and features one bedroom, a separate lounge, a kitchenette, a bathroom, a garage, and a carport. It’s an appealing seaside bolthole, a lock-up-and-leave Auckland base, or a rental investment to hold while you plan your next move. There’s also the option to explore its potential as holiday accommodation, subject to applicable requirements.\r\n\r\nFor builders and developers, the land is the standout. Flat, freehold and a manageable size, it’s an opportunity to create a quality family home in a premium coastal setting. Alternatively, investigate the potential for a two-home development, subject to council approval.\r\n\r\nTucked away in a peaceful pocket of the peninsula, you’re well placed to enjoy Eastern Beach, Bucklands Beach, local reserves and the nearby golf course. Surrounded by quality homes, this is a neighbourhood where lifestyle and location go hand in hand.\r\n\r\nTransport options are handy too, with bus stops on Bucklands Beach Road and Half Moon Bay Marina within easy reach. Catch the ferry into the city for work or leisure, then come home to life by the beach.\r\n\r\nWhether you’re looking for a weekend escape, a land bank investment or your next building project, this is an opportunity well worth exploring.\r\n\r\nFor sale by negotiation. Our motivated vendor wants this sold. Call now to arrange your viewing and bring us your offer!",
